        },
        "provenance_checksum": "sha256:0938c1d2576cdfa89bc1da6fbc1e595e9b48cdbc7a9007c1807ac3a01b0368ab",
        "rerank_rank": 4,
        "rerank_score": 0.25925925925925924,
        "title": "Merchant onboarding checklist",
        "vector_rank": 2,
        "vector_score": 0.5264087021181424
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "artifact_rate_limit_policy",
        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_rate_limit_policy_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_03bcc2c7f755f447d2a3d325",
        "content": "# Public API rate limit policy (synthetic) Owner: Developer Platform. Classification: public. Sandbox keys are limited to 10 requests per second per key with a burst allowance of 30. Production keys are limited to 200 requests per second per merchant account with a burst of 500. Limits are enforced per merchant account, not per key, so rotating keys does not raise a ceiling. Requests over the limit return HTTP 429 with a Retry-After header in whole seconds. Clients are expected to honor Retry-After and apply exponential backoff with jitter. Retrying a 429 without backoff is the single most common cause of a merchant remaining throttled. Rate limiting is independent of authorization outcomes. A throttled request was never routed to an acquirer and must not be treated as a decline.",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:d93d413404f9f6e2e50364977efec96241f162522b1a315bdca3b8650744e2bc",
        "fused_rank": 4,
        "fused_score": 0.031009615384615385,
        "lexical_rank": 4,
        "lexical_score": 22.0,
        "position": {
          "kind": "section",
          "locator": "limits"
        },
        "provenance_checksum": "sha256:9572b2366685ee087f632f70aa3f5cd67b1b8efdf88fec4d728b28fa913c0d18",
        "rerank_rank": 5,
        "rerank_score": 0.25925925925925924,
        "title": "Public API rate limit policy",
        "vector_rank": 5,
        "vector_score": 0.416704716679683
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "artifact_issuer_routing_spec",
        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_issuer_routing_spec_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_ebdeb648b43a5d27fc3ba6de",
        "content": "# Issuer routing v3 design specification (synthetic) Owner: Payments Platform. Status: shipped 2026-07-15. Routing v3 replaces the static issuer BIN table with a weighted scorer. Each authorization request is scored against issuer acceptance rate over a trailing 30-minute window, and the top-scoring acquirer path is selected. When the trailing window holds fewer than 40 samples the scorer falls back to the static table rather than routing on thin data. The known regression surface is the fallback boundary. If the sample counter is reset by a partial deploy, the scorer can hold a stale acceptance rate while believing the window is warm, which routes traffic to a degraded acquirer. Error code PYM-431 is emitted when the selected acquirer returns a soft decline that v3 does not retry. Rollback is a configuration flip of routing.engine.version back to v2. It does not require a binary redeploy and takes effect within one config propagation cycle.",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:0a4ac405988af9a8a37561dd8b75eb2a76018de1a69c31acc582619898a7e6e3",
        "fused_rank": 5,
        "fused_score": 0.030798389007344232,
        "lexical_rank": 3,
        "lexical_score": 24.0,
        "position": {
          "kind": "section",
          "locator": "fallback-boundary"
        },
        "provenance_checksum": "sha256:6c9d4ec9b2678a6c983a5d3463ba10c5f0a2ece50e3fc1a1590b4c1f95d7bf3c",
        "rerank_rank": 6,
        "rerank_score": 0.2222222222222222,
        "title": "Issuer routing v3 design specification",
        "vector_rank": 7,
        "vector_score": 0.2695459710502768
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "artifact_settlement_reconciliation",
        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_settlement_reconciliation_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_6501ce5ae6df0e9a1e139e64",
        "content": "# Nightly settlement reconciliation guide (synthetic) Owner: Settlement Engineering. Reconciliation runs at 02:00 ca-central and matches acquirer settlement files against internal authorization records for the prior banking day. Matching is keyed on the acquirer settlement reference, never on amount and timestamp, because same-amount transactions within a second are common at merchant scale. Three outcomes are possible per row: matched, internal-only, and acquirer-only. Internal-only rows older than two banking days are escalated to Settlement Engineering. Acquirer-only rows are almost always a late file and clear on the next run. A failed reconciliation run must be rerun from the same input file rather than regenerated. Regenerating the file changes the reference set and has previously produced duplicate records.",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:52a52dd1097b948cdb622ea5f8f9c2433005f61a7561ccb79074280aabdfc992",
        "fused_rank": 6,
        "fused_score": 0.030536130536130537,
        "lexical_rank": 5,
        "lexical_score": 20.0,
        "position": {
          "kind": "section",
          "locator": "match-outcomes"
        },
        "provenance_checksum": "sha256:26dc135f457db806fedaa0f4aaa9cc8eae0f86291ff17930642165fdae6702c9",
        "rerank_rank": 7,
        "rerank_score": 0.2222222222222222,
        "title": "Nightly settlement reconciliation guide",
        "vector_rank": 6,
        "vector_score": 0.40965086540936996
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "artifact_prior_incident_0987",
        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_prior_incident_0987_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_6dec7272256cf17edffb90ae",
        "content": "{\"error_code\":\"STL-208\",\"incident_id\":\"INC-0987\",\"not_related_to\":\"issuer routing or authorization decline handling\",\"opened_at\":\"2026-05-12T03:40:00Z\",\"resolution\":\"Deduplicated by acquirer reference and added a unique constraint. The worker now upserts on the reference key.\",\"resolved_at\":\"2026-05-12T09:15:00Z\",\"root_cause\":\"The reconciliation worker used a non-idempotent insert keyed on a timestamp rather than the acquirer chargeback reference.\",\"route\":\"Settlement Engineering\",\"service\":\"settlement-worker\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"summary\":\"A reconciliation job retried after a partial write and created duplicate chargeback rows for 1,412 synthetic transactions. Merchant balances were overstated for six hours.\",\"tenant\":\"HelioPay (fictional)\",\"title\":\"Duplicate chargeback records after reconciliation retry\"}",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:f0f8a6bf978b8ea74083aecc30296866119fa56a07bc41bbb0bdc5ba81a5da54",
        "fused_rank": 7,
        "fused_score": 0.030117753623188408,
        "lexical_rank": 9,
        "lexical_score": 13.0,
        "position": {
          "kind": "row",
          "locator": "incident-0987"
        },
        "provenance_checksum": "sha256:df2bff2ac8892aaf6f88c995adeebd315985a0edab027c1326f9cee1f504ade6",
        "rerank_rank": 8,
        "rerank_score": 0.18518518518518517,
        "title": "Prior incident 0987 chargeback duplication",
        "vector_rank": 4,
        "vector_score": 0.45358299068301866
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "artifact_mobile_sdk_changelog",
        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_mobile_sdk_changelog_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_c0081a6c57e29b31fbd176ff",
        "content": "# Mobile SDK changelog (synthetic) Owner: Client Platform. Version 8.4.0, 2026-07-09. Adds network token refresh on foreground. Fixes a retry loop where a 429 from the rate limiter was treated as a transient network failure and retried immediately. Version 8.3.2, 2026-06-21. Fixes a crash when the device clock is more than 24 hours behind, which invalidated request signing. Adds a clock-skew warning to the SDK log. Version 8.3.0, 2026-05-30. Introduces the deferred capture API. Deprecates the legacy charge endpoint, which remains available through 2027-01-01. The SDK does not implement issuer routing and is unaffected by routing engine version changes. Client-side symptoms of a routing regression appear as elevated soft declines, not as SDK errors.",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:56fb9a19cd809ede980f600d607984d8b8e73ae0f14d3b8981bb544399a15d9b",
        "fused_rank": 9,
        "fused_score": 0.02919863597612958,
        "lexical_rank": 8,
        "lexical_score": 14.0,
        "position": {
